  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 254 PM CDT Thu Jul 30 2026\n\nA cooler and drier airmass will move in behind the\naforementioned cold front on Saturday. In fact, high\ntemperatures are only progged to reach the mid 70s to low 80s,\nwhich is around 10 to 15 degrees below the climatological\naverage. A well mixed thermo profile and modest surface pressure\ngradient will support breezy northerly winds as well, with\nfrequent gusts of 25 to 30 mph. \n\nEnsemble clusters depict varying solutions in how quickly they\npivot Friday's system through the northeastern CONUS;\nregardless, it will largely be out of influence for our CWA. At\nmost, the eastern Ozarks could experience a few showers behind\nthe low on Monday and Tuesday should the slower solution pan out.\nOut west, the flattened ridge will persist throughout much of \nthe week. This will keep precipitation chances low with no \nobvious signal for widespread rainfall.",
